# Changelog

All notable changes to SPDL (Semantic Process Definition Language) will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

## [0.1] - 2026-06-03

### Added
- Initial SPDL specification (v0.1)
- Core 4-layer semantic framework:
  - Layer 1: Process Model (activities, decisions, variants)
  - Layer 2: Semantic Layer (concepts, definitions, relationships)
  - Layer 3: Knowledge Layer (business rules, risks, controls)
  - Layer 4: Agent Layer (AI blueprints, execution specs)
- JSON Schema specification (spdl-schema-v0.1.json)
- Example processes:
  - Goods Receipt (SAP MM)
  - Invoice Processing (Finance)
  - Sponsorship Process (Business Development)
- Dual license
- Comprehensive README and documentation

### Documentation
- README with quick start guide
- SPDL schema with property descriptions
- Example SPDL documents with real process data
- Use case documentation

## Planned for [0.2] - Q3 2026

### Planned
- YAML format support
- XML export capability
- Validation tooling and CLI
- Additional examples (10+ processes)
- GitHub organization templates
- Community contribution guidelines

## Planned for [1.0] - Q4 2026

### Planned
- Official specification release
- Multiple language support
- Industry standards alignment (BPMN, OCPM)
- Complete toolkit release
- Enterprise features

